WEBVTT

00:19.560 --> 00:23.260
<i>Gokusen</i>

00:23.530 --> 00:28.760
<i>How long has it been</i>
<i>since that day when we first met?</i>

00:28.930 --> 00:34.460
<i>So many good times and bad times</i>
<i>have come and gone since then.</i>

00:34.640 --> 00:39.810
<i>I know you can't make sense</i>
<i>of what I'm trying to say.</i>

00:39.980 --> 00:45.210
<i>But my true feelings for you</i>
<i>can never be put into words.</i>

00:45.520 --> 00:50.980
<i>Will you ever know how I feel? Will you</i>
<i>ever know what's going on inside me?</i>

00:51.190 --> 00:56.630
<i>If only we could live in a world where</i>
<i>you only have to be yourself and smile.</i>

00:56.790 --> 01:02.060
<i>Or is it always going to be like this?</i>
<i>Will we be able to go on like this?</i>

01:02.270 --> 01:09.970
<i>Even if you're far away, I want to</i>
<i>feel you in my heart, close to me.</i>

01:22.920 --> 01:25.250
Oh crap! I'm gonna be late!

01:38.400 --> 01:39.060
Hey, hey!

01:39.340 --> 01:42.870
Who would've thought...
the Principal's tardy too!

01:43.210 --> 01:44.470
Principal...

01:45.580 --> 01:48.210
Good morning...

01:51.350 --> 01:53.820
Holy crap, he's supersized!

01:54.050 --> 01:57.890
Hey, you! Baldie!
So you were a monster after all?

01:58.090 --> 01:59.650
Chairman, look out!

01:59.890 --> 02:00.950
How dare you?

02:01.060 --> 02:01.860
Vice Principal...

02:01.960 --> 02:04.290
This is the Chairman!
What do you think you're doing?

02:04.400 --> 02:06.130
Huh? No!

02:06.830 --> 02:11.790
<i>SHIROKIN HIGH CLOSING...!?</i>

02:13.640 --> 02:15.630
This is my older brother.

02:15.740 --> 02:18.440
Not to mention the
Chairman of our school.

02:18.640 --> 02:20.040
I apologize.

02:20.180 --> 02:22.840
I had no idea, but still...

02:22.980 --> 02:26.110
As the teacher is, so is the student.

02:26.250 --> 02:31.380
Well, I guess you could say that
she's the perfect match for those losers.

02:32.220 --> 02:32.920
What?

02:33.020 --> 02:36.460
Never mind, now! You are
free to go now, Ms. Yamaguchi.

02:36.560 --> 02:38.090
Please excuse me.

02:38.200 --> 02:40.320
What a nasty old coot!

02:40.900 --> 02:43.930
So anyway...
Brother, what brings you here today?

02:44.800 --> 02:48.000
What? You're closing down
Shirokin High School?

02:48.910 --> 02:51.880
We won't be taking any
applications for next year...

02:51.980 --> 02:54.500
That's been decided by
the Board of Directors.

02:54.610 --> 02:56.880
Well! So I take it that means...

02:57.110 --> 02:59.550
You mean to say that
Shirokin High is to be...

02:59.620 --> 03:01.050
That's right.

03:01.490 --> 03:04.350
Shirokin High School will be closed!

03:05.560 --> 03:07.080
But that's...

03:07.190 --> 03:10.960
You shouldn't be surprised.
Every year enrollment is down...

03:11.130 --> 03:12.860
...while our deficit soars!

03:12.960 --> 03:16.530
But how can you close down a
school with so much tradition?

03:16.630 --> 03:17.800
Tradition?

03:17.940 --> 03:21.900
This place is crawling with losers,
certainly not tradition!

03:22.010 --> 03:25.500
If it were a school renowned
for academics or athletics...

03:25.610 --> 03:28.040
...then perhaps one could
say it had tradition.

03:28.180 --> 03:33.620
But look what we have here! The students
here have no abilities, no motivation...

03:33.680 --> 03:35.180
They're bottom-feeders...

03:35.290 --> 03:36.950
Now just a damn minute, you!

03:37.050 --> 03:38.550
Ms. Yamaguchi!

03:38.660 --> 03:40.120
What do you want?

03:40.220 --> 03:41.890
What are you still doing here?

03:41.990 --> 03:44.390
What did you just say, you bald freak?

03:44.530 --> 03:47.330
Our students are bottom-feeders, huh?

03:47.500 --> 03:50.090
Huh? Who the hell do you think you are?

03:50.800 --> 03:54.360
It's all about grades and
trophies, is that it? Huh?

03:54.470 --> 03:57.100
Ms. Yamaguchi! You're way out of line!

03:57.840 --> 04:00.640
That's right.
That's what it's all about.

04:00.810 --> 04:01.570
Hah!

04:02.280 --> 04:06.440
There's something way more
important than that in this world!

04:06.580 --> 04:07.750
Right here...

04:07.990 --> 04:09.610
...in the pit of your stomach!

04:09.720 --> 04:12.210
The pit of your stomach?

04:12.320 --> 04:14.690
What in the world do you mean?

04:14.890 --> 04:15.880
For chrissake...

04:16.030 --> 04:19.590
You two brothers are bald as hell
and don't have a frickin' clue!

04:20.100 --> 04:24.160
The Divinity of Fire who
resides in your belly...DUH!

04:24.540 --> 04:26.090
Divinity of Fire?

04:26.370 --> 04:28.240
I have no idea what
you're talking about.

04:28.340 --> 04:31.100
But that's certainly no way
to run a high school...

04:31.480 --> 04:33.380
Absolutely not!

04:33.610 --> 04:34.940
All right, then...

04:35.080 --> 04:38.240
All they have to do is make a name
for themselves, for Shirokin, right?

04:38.380 --> 04:40.010
Not going to happen.

04:40.350 --> 04:43.720
Those kids have the potential
to accomplish anything!

04:44.260 --> 04:46.020
Whether it's in sports or whatever...

04:46.120 --> 04:48.960
...they could even be No. 1 in Japan
if they set their minds to it!

04:49.030 --> 04:49.890
Impossible.

04:49.990 --> 04:50.790
They can do it!

04:50.900 --> 04:52.360
They don't have a chance.

04:53.730 --> 04:54.790
Oh, yes they do.

04:54.900 --> 04:56.600
If I say it's impossible,
it's impossible!

04:56.700 --> 04:59.430
If they do pull it off, then what?
Will you call off closing the school?

04:59.540 --> 05:01.630
Sure, if they pull it off!

05:01.740 --> 05:02.370
Hmm!

05:02.810 --> 05:03.710
All right...

05:03.870 --> 05:07.280
How about putting that
in writing, then, like a contract?

05:07.380 --> 05:08.070
Huh?

05:08.210 --> 05:10.980
That's ridiculous!
All I meant just now was...

05:11.120 --> 05:13.350
Are you saying you can't
even keep your word?

05:14.590 --> 05:17.490
That kind of thing is
called double-crossing...

05:17.760 --> 05:19.490
...where I come from!

05:22.530 --> 05:24.190
<i>CONTRACT</i>

05:24.300 --> 05:26.630
So you ended up with this agreement?

05:26.760 --> 05:28.360
I guess I did!

05:28.530 --> 05:30.690
"No. 1 in Japan in any kind of way..."

05:30.840 --> 05:34.070
"However, this is restricted to
either academic or athletic pursuits."

05:34.170 --> 05:37.270
And we only have until the deadline
to release our application guidelines...

05:37.370 --> 05:38.810
...2 weeks from now!

05:38.910 --> 05:40.670
Still, you did a good job!

05:40.880 --> 05:42.350
Mr. Iwamoto...

05:42.480 --> 05:45.420
Even if we only have 2 weeks,
it's better to do whatever we can.

05:45.550 --> 05:46.540
Yes, you're right...

05:46.750 --> 05:49.650
All right, let's figure out
what we can do about this.

05:49.750 --> 05:52.220
We all feel the same way about Shirokin!

05:52.320 --> 05:53.120
Right!

05:53.590 --> 05:54.720
All of you...

05:55.790 --> 05:59.820
You might not know it, but
I was a rugby player in college.

05:59.930 --> 06:04.200
I will start a rugby team and go for No. 1
in next week's national tournament!

06:05.840 --> 06:08.170
I'm going for the
one-on-one approach.

06:08.270 --> 06:10.170
So you're a judo expert, Mr. Hatta?

06:10.270 --> 06:11.770
No, karate, actually.

06:12.280 --> 06:15.080
I've been waiting for the chance
to train young Tsuruta.

06:15.180 --> 06:16.240
Oh, that's right!

06:16.310 --> 06:17.940
I forgot that we had Tsuruta!

06:18.080 --> 06:20.240
I've thought long and hard about this.

06:20.380 --> 06:22.980
Mr. Kohda? What's with
that cap you've got on?

06:23.550 --> 06:25.180
Actually, back in the day...

06:25.660 --> 06:28.720
I was a candidate for the
Olympic Water Polo Team!

06:28.830 --> 06:29.760
Behold!

06:29.860 --> 06:30.730
Whoa!

06:31.660 --> 06:34.460
Well, you certainly
have the physique for it!

06:34.570 --> 06:37.470
Ugh, I can't stand to see,
ripply muscles...

06:37.700 --> 06:41.040
If one of our students is named to
the World Junior Water Polo Tournament...

06:41.140 --> 06:45.470
...then that should
prove that we're No. 1!

06:46.710 --> 06:49.610
Okay. I'm just as determined
as the rest of you.

06:49.750 --> 06:52.740
My Choir Club will triumph
at the national competition!

06:52.850 --> 06:54.650
Good for you! I know you can do it!

06:54.950 --> 06:56.220
All right, then! Let's do it!

06:56.320 --> 06:56.950
Right!

06:59.220 --> 07:02.020
Everyone has some kind of hidden talent...

07:02.330 --> 07:04.300
Yes, but Ms. Yamaguchi...

07:04.400 --> 07:05.020
What?

07:05.300 --> 07:08.270
Do you really think we have a chance?

07:08.570 --> 07:09.360
Uh...

07:11.300 --> 07:14.830
You gotta be kidding us. There's
no way in hell that's gonna happen!

07:14.940 --> 07:16.570
Are you retarded?

07:16.670 --> 07:20.130
I told you! Unless we do something,
the school's going to be closed!

07:20.310 --> 07:22.340
Yeah, after we've graduated!

07:22.480 --> 07:23.780
What are you talking about?

07:23.910 --> 07:26.440
They're closing down your
alma mater. That's a sad thing!

07:26.520 --> 07:27.990
Who gives a rat's ass?

07:28.090 --> 07:32.050
When you guys have all grown old
and bald in a few decades you won't...

07:32.160 --> 07:36.120
...be able to dig up your time capsules
because this school will be gone!

07:36.230 --> 07:36.960
So what?

07:37.060 --> 07:38.860
Not gonna bury anything anyway.

07:40.660 --> 07:42.260
What should I do?

07:42.370 --> 07:43.930
How should I know?

07:44.200 --> 07:47.370
Why are you asking
me stuff like that, anyhow?

07:48.110 --> 07:49.330
Well...

07:50.140 --> 07:54.100
I'm the one who started all this,
but I can't think of anything...

07:54.880 --> 07:56.440
Let me think...

07:56.850 --> 08:00.510
...the only thing you're really
good at is brawling, I guess.

08:00.750 --> 08:02.910
Look here, you!

08:03.150 --> 08:05.450
I'm asking you a serious question!

08:05.660 --> 08:07.630
I gave you a serious answer.

08:07.890 --> 08:09.050
Let's face it...

08:09.160 --> 08:12.720
The one thing this school has a chance
of beating anybody at is a fight.

08:12.860 --> 08:14.530
Well, this is true.

08:15.000 --> 08:18.960
And this might be the right time
to get into an all-out fight, too.

08:19.100 --> 08:21.070
What the hell are you talking about?

08:21.940 --> 08:22.910
Never mind.

08:23.040 --> 08:24.670
What is it? Spit it out!

08:25.240 --> 08:26.970
All right, then, I'll tell you.

08:27.310 --> 08:29.800
The reason the chairman wants
to shut down this school is...

08:29.950 --> 08:32.470
...because he wants to build a
new office building on this site.

08:32.550 --> 08:33.310
Huh?

08:34.150 --> 08:35.410
The Vice Principal...

08:35.520 --> 08:38.490
I hear he's already got a
new job in the bag there.

08:38.820 --> 08:41.920
What the hell? That sonofabitch!

08:42.060 --> 08:44.030
You only noticed now?

08:44.930 --> 08:47.060
So give it a shot. A massive brawl...

08:47.160 --> 08:49.430
No, a contract is a contract!

08:49.530 --> 08:51.870
We're gonna to become No. 1
in Japan, fair and square...

08:51.970 --> 08:54.130
...and then we're gonna
rub it in their faces!

08:56.440 --> 08:57.640
Yeah, well...

08:57.910 --> 09:00.430
...that's more your style anyway.

09:01.880 --> 09:03.710
Easier said than done...

09:03.780 --> 09:05.440
No. 1 in Japan, huh?

09:05.950 --> 09:08.940
The question is, what to try for No. 1 in.

09:11.990 --> 09:12.580
Huh?

09:13.090 --> 09:14.290
What the hell's going on?

09:14.830 --> 09:16.620
Please! I beg of you!

09:17.160 --> 09:18.960
For chrissake, you're here again?

09:19.230 --> 09:20.390
What a pest!

09:20.500 --> 09:23.190
Oh, please, hear me out! I beg of you!

09:23.530 --> 09:26.330
You better cut it out right now
or I'll kill you!

09:26.440 --> 09:29.130
What's up? Is that guy here again?

09:29.240 --> 09:31.000
Oh, Ojou! Welcome home.

09:31.480 --> 09:35.780
I've told him over and over that we're not
looking for any new cugines right now.

09:35.850 --> 09:37.970
This is the fourth time since last week!

09:38.120 --> 09:40.580
A guy like you with no skills, get lost!

09:40.720 --> 09:42.450
But I do have skills! I do!

09:42.590 --> 09:44.890
Just as I informed you the other day...

09:45.090 --> 09:47.390
What was it again? His skill?

09:47.590 --> 09:49.460
Uh, you know! He was in Mexico...

09:49.590 --> 09:52.320
Right! I did some
professional boxing there...

09:52.460 --> 09:54.830
Huh? But that's perfect!

10:00.000 --> 10:02.230
<i>Would the following students...</i>

10:02.340 --> 10:05.170
<i>...please report immediately to</i>
<i>the storage house by the gym?</i>

10:05.280 --> 10:09.840
<i>From Class 2-4, Shin Sawada,</i>
<i>Teruo Kumai, Yoichi Minami...</i>

10:10.280 --> 10:14.720
<i>... Takeshi Noda, and Haruhiko Uchiyama.</i>
<i>That's it!</i>

10:15.890 --> 10:17.850
<i>BOXING TEAM</i>

10:16.320 --> 10:17.850
I'm gonna kill her!

10:18.220 --> 10:20.210
What the hell is she thinking,
for chrissake?

10:20.720 --> 10:22.660
Hey there! You're all here.

10:22.830 --> 10:25.960
Listen, Yamaguchi. Who says
I'm gonna be your captain, huh?

10:26.100 --> 10:28.220
Who cares? I'm just using your name.

10:28.330 --> 10:30.160
It doesn't matter who's captain, anyway.

10:30.270 --> 10:32.400
Yeah, but I never joined this team!

10:32.500 --> 10:33.530
Attaboy!

10:33.670 --> 10:35.640
The wolf must clench his fist!

10:35.740 --> 10:37.500
You're dead, goddammit.

10:37.740 --> 10:39.040
Boxing, huh?

10:39.280 --> 10:40.680
I kinda like the idea...

10:41.040 --> 10:43.210
You can smack people all you want...

10:43.310 --> 10:44.300
I'm sold!

10:44.410 --> 10:45.620
Good point...

10:45.120 --> 10:46.680
For you...

10:46.820 --> 10:49.050
My budding pugilists,
I've even hired an expert coach.

10:49.150 --> 10:50.680
Coach? Over here, please!

10:51.260 --> 10:54.520
Former professional boxer,
Coach Norio Maruta!

10:55.860 --> 10:58.330
His ring name was Carlos Shou!

10:58.460 --> 11:00.120
Whoa!

11:00.300 --> 11:04.290
Hey, Yankumi! He looks like a yakuza...
and that's a generous view!

11:04.400 --> 11:06.870
Where the hell did you
find a dude like that?

11:06.970 --> 11:10.130
What are you talking about?
He's just an ordinary guy.

11:10.310 --> 11:15.140
Uh...Coach? When you were in the ring,
how far did you go?

11:15.380 --> 11:16.850
Like in the rankings?

11:17.580 --> 11:23.280
Well, Hanheri Gomegomez, the former
Mexican WQA champion once asked...

11:23.420 --> 11:26.390
...me to throw my match
against him, and I did.

11:26.690 --> 11:28.350
That's supposed to be impressive, huh?

11:28.430 --> 11:31.690
You little dumbasses, what could be
more impressive, dammit?

11:31.800 --> 11:35.060
If I hadn't thrown the match,
I would've defeated the champion!

11:35.200 --> 11:38.190
All right, all right,
now that we're all here...

11:38.300 --> 11:39.030
Seriously?

11:39.140 --> 11:40.040
No way!

11:41.040 --> 11:41.940
So?

11:42.310 --> 11:45.900
How are we going to get to
No. 1 in less than 2 weeks?

11:46.010 --> 11:49.100
Damn right. You got some kind of
kickass secret plan or something?

11:49.210 --> 11:50.610
Well, here's the thing.

11:50.850 --> 11:55.050
The National High School Boxing
Tournament just ended the other day...

11:55.150 --> 11:57.210
Huh? Then it's no good!

11:57.320 --> 11:58.520
However...

11:58.790 --> 12:02.950
I've decided to challenge the winner
of the tourney, Yabuki High, to a match!

12:03.060 --> 12:04.590
Y-Yabuki High?

12:04.700 --> 12:07.820
Even amateurs like us have heard
of their killer boxing squad!

12:07.930 --> 12:13.230
If we can beat the No. 1 boxing team
in Japan in any way, no one will dispute us!

12:13.340 --> 12:14.860
Who's gonna buy that bullshit?

12:14.940 --> 12:15.870
They'll buy it!

12:17.140 --> 12:20.670
We have a better chance of beating
them than winning the Nationals.

12:20.780 --> 12:22.540
You're right there, but...

12:22.680 --> 12:24.050
So, when's it gonna be?

12:24.180 --> 12:26.210
The match? They turned me down.

12:26.350 --> 12:27.050
Hey!

12:27.150 --> 12:30.950
They said they don't have time
to play with amateurs like us.

12:31.290 --> 12:33.480
What a bunch of arrogant pricks.

12:33.590 --> 12:36.620
I'm going to try to
convince them to take us on.

12:36.730 --> 12:38.220
So train your asses off!

12:38.330 --> 12:39.060
Right!

12:45.000 --> 12:48.230
They think a little cramming
will take them to No. 1?

12:48.840 --> 12:51.810
Go on, keep up your futile struggle.

12:57.310 --> 12:58.750
Hey, it's a punching ball!

12:58.820 --> 12:59.480
Wow...

12:59.580 --> 13:00.780
Let's hang it up...

13:02.920 --> 13:04.550
What the hell are you doing?

13:04.660 --> 13:05.620
Carlos!

13:07.290 --> 13:09.760
Carlos! What the hell's going on?

13:11.500 --> 13:12.790
But, Ms. Yamaguchi.

13:12.900 --> 13:15.420
If we train the normal way, we're
not going to stand a chance of...

13:15.530 --> 13:17.330
...winning in just two weeks.

13:17.570 --> 13:19.130
So here's my idea.

13:19.270 --> 13:21.830
Just hit them, and hit them
until they're used to getting hit...

13:21.940 --> 13:23.840
...to keep them from falling down!

13:23.940 --> 13:25.640
Well, you do have a point.

13:25.740 --> 13:26.300
Huh?

13:26.480 --> 13:28.640
Come on, we'll be killed first!

13:29.550 --> 13:30.510
Listen up!

13:30.580 --> 13:34.040
In a boxing match, it's just as
important to scare your opponent.

13:34.150 --> 13:36.380
When you stare each other
down for the first time...

13:36.490 --> 13:38.150
...if you can scare him into oblivion.

13:38.220 --> 13:40.880
Then that improves your
chances of winning by 9 percent!

13:40.990 --> 13:43.830
9 percent? That's it?

13:43.960 --> 13:45.590
I think he means 90 percent.

13:45.700 --> 13:48.460
Are you listening?
This is how you do it!

13:51.100 --> 13:52.400
No good, no good!

13:52.570 --> 13:56.200
You look like a bunch of old men
choking on their rice cakes!

14:01.810 --> 14:02.780
Hello?

14:03.010 --> 14:06.450
This is Yamaguchi of Shirokin High School,
we spoke earlier...

14:06.580 --> 14:08.020
So it's you again?

14:08.550 --> 14:10.490
You need to stop this right now.

14:10.690 --> 14:12.520
We're the national champions.

14:12.820 --> 14:14.690
We're way out of your school's league.

14:14.790 --> 14:16.260
But is there any way...

14:16.390 --> 14:17.590
No, it's impossible.

14:17.730 --> 14:21.460
We're going into training camp
with a college team.

14:23.530 --> 14:25.560
So he turned you down again?

14:26.000 --> 14:26.900
Yeah...

14:26.970 --> 14:27.960
It's no good.

14:28.070 --> 14:30.370
What's the matter, Mr. Iwamoto?

14:30.470 --> 14:32.880
The whole rugby team's injured.

14:32.980 --> 14:33.810
What?

14:34.080 --> 14:36.600
I got carried away with their training.

14:37.080 --> 14:38.100
So sorry.

14:38.750 --> 14:43.410
Unfortunately, the water polo team's
going to have to forfeit.

14:43.890 --> 14:45.520
What in the world happened?

14:46.260 --> 14:49.660
If any of them gets hold of the ball,
they can't stay afloat.

14:49.760 --> 14:54.130
If I made them compete now...
I fear there would be casualties...

14:54.560 --> 14:58.060
Well, we still have hopes for
tomorrow's choir competition and...

14:58.170 --> 15:00.160
...the karate tournament the next day.

15:00.270 --> 15:03.670
<i>62nd Tokyo Choir Competition</i>

15:05.710 --> 15:08.680
<i>JUDGES</i>

15:16.120 --> 15:17.880
How dare they?

15:17.990 --> 15:21.420
<i>Unique Character Award</i>

15:17.990 --> 15:19.420
What kind of a prize is this?

15:19.520 --> 15:21.420
It's not a costume parade!

15:21.790 --> 15:24.420
We're screwed.
Now our backs are against the wall!

15:24.530 --> 15:25.500
Stop pestering!

15:25.600 --> 15:29.050
We're training with the college squad
both tomorrow and the day after!

15:30.200 --> 15:31.830
Come on, Tsuruta!

15:31.940 --> 15:34.560
If you stay calm, you can beat anyone!

15:40.140 --> 15:40.870
Thanks.

15:41.780 --> 15:44.750
Tsuruta only made it to the quarterfinals.

15:47.980 --> 15:51.440
Only one more day to go,
then all of you will have failed!

15:51.560 --> 15:55.360
And then I shall become an
executive of the new company!

15:58.130 --> 16:00.430
Come on, cugines! Get yourselves ready!

16:01.500 --> 16:02.830
We're hitting the mattresses!

16:02.930 --> 16:05.840
<i>RIKIISHI COLLEGE</i>

16:05.970 --> 16:10.870
Give it all you've got, now. It's not like
we're up against some loser school...

16:12.510 --> 16:13.270
Huh?

16:13.410 --> 16:14.880
It's dark in here...

16:16.080 --> 16:18.950
The Shirokin High Boxing Team is here!

16:20.080 --> 16:22.380
What the hell? Huh?

16:23.650 --> 16:25.250
What's going on?

16:26.360 --> 16:29.760
The boys on the college boxing team
are a cool bunch.

16:29.990 --> 16:32.330
They were kind enough
to give up their slot...

16:32.400 --> 16:35.020
...so that our team could
take yours on in a match!

16:36.500 --> 16:38.590
All right! We're dead serious.

16:39.140 --> 16:41.130
We won't take no for an answer!

16:44.240 --> 16:46.230
Let's go! Minami, you kick his butt!

16:46.340 --> 16:49.040
The face! Don't forget to make a face!

16:49.880 --> 16:51.820
Good! It's working!

16:57.250 --> 16:58.980
Sudden death?

16:59.090 --> 17:00.520
Crap!

17:01.060 --> 17:02.550
Next! Noda!

17:08.200 --> 17:11.460
That's 2 losses already, Carlos.
We can't lose any more!

17:11.840 --> 17:13.030
This isn't good.

17:13.200 --> 17:15.170
Come on, pull yourselves together!

17:15.270 --> 17:16.210
Uchi!

17:17.210 --> 17:18.270
Is it okay...

17:18.610 --> 17:21.040
...if I batter my opponent senseless?

17:28.450 --> 17:30.610
Come on...Bring it!

17:31.620 --> 17:33.060
Coach...

17:33.160 --> 17:35.460
Just finish him off as fast as you can.

17:39.630 --> 17:41.620
It's over, man.

17:42.470 --> 17:43.060
Huh!

17:43.170 --> 17:44.130
He got up!

17:46.300 --> 17:47.100
One...

17:47.600 --> 17:48.400
Two...

17:55.350 --> 17:57.940
The punching ball training's
really paying off!

17:58.150 --> 17:59.340
It's paying off too much!

17:59.480 --> 18:01.510
Uchi, that's enough. Don't get up!

18:02.020 --> 18:03.990
Son, are you all right?

18:05.120 --> 18:05.920
Son...

18:11.530 --> 18:14.290
Great, that's a knockout! Uchi wins!

18:14.400 --> 18:16.630
Like hell! That one doesn't count!
It's invalid!

18:16.730 --> 18:17.790
You shut up!

18:18.000 --> 18:20.300
Anyone can see it's a knockout!

18:20.400 --> 18:23.200
If you don't like it,
we'll show you where to put it!

18:23.340 --> 18:24.900
You'll show me where to...?

18:25.010 --> 18:26.940
Never mind! Next match!

18:27.680 --> 18:29.510
Shin-boy, hold up a sec.

18:29.610 --> 18:30.410
What is it?

18:31.250 --> 18:33.880
Don't tell me at this late stage
that you have some kind of plan?

18:34.020 --> 18:35.280
Actually, I do.

18:35.550 --> 18:38.180
We're not here to play a sport.

18:38.690 --> 18:41.280
This is a fight that we can't lose!

18:41.460 --> 18:42.360
Yamaguchi...

18:42.490 --> 18:43.390
Take a look.

18:43.530 --> 18:46.520
The referee is still out of it
from that blow he took.

18:46.830 --> 18:48.460
I don't care what you do...

18:48.830 --> 18:51.300
...just make sure you win this fight!

18:51.600 --> 18:55.130
Chrissake, that doesn't
sound like a teacher talking!

18:55.240 --> 18:56.730
But hey, I gotcha.

18:57.870 --> 18:58.970
Take that!

19:00.380 --> 19:02.040
Hey, he fouled him!

19:02.180 --> 19:03.010
Referee!

19:05.050 --> 19:06.520
Stop screaming at me...

19:06.650 --> 19:08.410
My head's about to split...

19:08.550 --> 19:09.750
'Scuse me?

19:10.020 --> 19:12.490
My guy's on the mat?

19:12.590 --> 19:14.150
Oh. Okay, okay.

19:15.160 --> 19:17.350
Shirokin High! Shin Sawada!

19:18.230 --> 19:19.530
Stop whining!

19:19.630 --> 19:22.260
The heavyweight match will decide all!
Kuma!

19:22.370 --> 19:23.260
Right.

19:24.070 --> 19:25.930
All right, no way are we losing now!

19:26.040 --> 19:28.230
I'm sending in our
exchange student, Bison!

19:34.640 --> 19:35.200
What!

19:35.550 --> 19:37.610
What the hell is this?

19:38.620 --> 19:40.380
Kuma can't beat that guy.

19:41.420 --> 19:43.580
Kuma, never mind this match...

19:44.450 --> 19:46.860
I want you two guys
to take the others home.

19:46.920 --> 19:47.620
Huh?

19:47.960 --> 19:48.690
Shin.

19:54.100 --> 19:56.090
All right. Let's go, Kuma.

19:56.570 --> 19:58.190
Huh? Okay.

19:58.700 --> 19:59.400
But...

19:59.500 --> 20:01.470
Just come on! We're going.

20:09.780 --> 20:10.750
Yamaguchi.

20:11.550 --> 20:14.250
Just how are you planning
to take care of this?

20:17.450 --> 20:20.010
New boxer for Shirokin High School.

20:20.290 --> 20:20.990
Ojou!

20:21.090 --> 20:21.890
Ojou!

20:22.130 --> 20:25.860
Now that it's come to this,
looks like it's anything-goes for you...

20:25.960 --> 20:27.260
But are you serious?

20:27.360 --> 20:29.490
Never been more serious in my life.

20:29.600 --> 20:32.500
This is a bona fide battle
for sheer survival!

20:35.000 --> 20:35.990
Come on!

20:39.210 --> 20:41.800
For chrissake,
bigger isn't always better!

20:43.550 --> 20:45.980
Vengeance is mine!

20:47.120 --> 20:49.140
<i>Shirokin High Boxing Team Defeats</i>
<i>Boxing Powerhouse Yabuki High...</i>

20:49.250 --> 20:51.310
<i>...In 1st Meeting For 1st Victory</i>
This, this means nothing!

20:51.690 --> 20:54.750
It was nothing but an informal match!

20:54.860 --> 20:55.880
Hey!

20:56.060 --> 20:58.650
If we beat the No. 1 team in Japan,
that makes us No. 1 in Japan...

20:58.760 --> 20:59.990
...in anyone's book!

21:00.100 --> 21:02.070
We've got a contract, remember?

21:02.170 --> 21:04.100
If you don't like it,
I'll show you where to put it!

21:04.200 --> 21:05.790
Little brother...

21:06.070 --> 21:08.770
That's what Ms. Yamaguchi
told me to tell you.

21:10.570 --> 21:13.040
That damned woman!

21:13.140 --> 21:17.840
Dammit! Thanks to Kumiko Yamaguchi,
I've lost my position as an executive!

21:17.950 --> 21:19.010
Curses!

21:19.450 --> 21:21.510
Huh? That's...

21:22.090 --> 21:22.950
Ojou!

21:23.090 --> 21:26.920
Thank you for crediting me
with the win in that last match.

21:27.090 --> 21:30.320
Because of that, I can now
hold my head up to those brats!

21:30.430 --> 21:32.400
Oh, hey, don't do that here.

21:32.800 --> 21:35.930
I'm going to put in a good word for you
about the Initiation Cup, okay?

21:36.030 --> 21:36.520
Huh?

21:36.800 --> 21:40.400
You mean I can become an
official member of the Ooedo Clan?

21:40.500 --> 21:43.470
Moron! Don't ever mention
that stuff here at school!

21:43.740 --> 21:46.900
Ooedo Clan? Initiation Cup?

21:47.180 --> 21:49.410
Not to mention, "Ojou"?

21:49.950 --> 21:52.210
What in the world...

22:07.530 --> 22:17.530
<i>We are all born</i>
<i>crying out to the world.</i>

22:18.580 --> 22:28.510
<i>Because of all the endless grief</i>
<i>that we must go through in life.</i>

22:29.290 --> 22:38.990
<i>All of the heartache</i>
<i>is such a heavy load to bear.</i>

22:39.300 --> 22:44.200
<i>On those days when</i>
<i>I am alone and cold...</i>

22:44.430 --> 22:49.340
<i>...I'll light a fire with</i>
<i>my own two hands.</i>

22:49.770 --> 22:54.680
<i>The treacherous mountains</i>
<i>are my chosen path.</i>

22:54.880 --> 23:01.610
<i>I'll keep moving forward</i>
<i>without a backward glance.</i>

23:16.430 --> 23:18.400
You did it again, Ojou!

23:18.500 --> 23:22.200
You've saved Shirokin
High from oblivion!

23:22.340 --> 23:25.640
Now nothing can stop you from
becoming the No. 1 teacher in Japan!

23:25.740 --> 23:27.340
I'm rooting for you!

23:27.440 --> 23:28.430
Whoops...

23:28.540 --> 23:31.240
No such luck, you say?

23:31.380 --> 23:34.150
Looks like there's still
some lowlifes around...

23:34.250 --> 23:37.910
...who won't stop till
they've thwarted you, Ojou.

23:38.150 --> 23:42.250
Next episode: the final:
Yankumi's Final Act of Honor!

23:42.430 --> 23:45.950
You give them the pounding they deserve!
